meta:
  id: sdg-knowledge-quiz-post
  name: SDG Knowledge Quiz (Post)
  version: 1.0.0
  description: |
    7-question multiple-choice knowledge check on SDG 4, 11, and 13,
    administered after the VR exploration. Identical content to the
    Pre-VR card so pre/post recall can be compared.
  shortName: SdgQuizPost
  tags: [knowledge, sdg, post]

questions:
  - id: sdg4_q1
    text: What is the aim of SDG 4?
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - Ensure inclusive, equitable quality education and lifelong learning for all
        - End hunger and improve nutrition
        - Make cities inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable
        - Conserve the oceans and marine resources

  - id: sdg4_q2
    text: According to the UN, accelerating progress on Goal 4 would have what effect?
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - A catalytic effect on the whole 2030 Agenda
        - No effect on other goals
        - It only affects high-income countries
        - It would slow progress on climate action

  - id: sdg11_q1
    text: SDG 11 aims to make cities and human settlements...
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable
        - larger and denser
        - centers of industrial production
        - car-free by 2030

  - id: sdg11_q2
    text: Helsinki's Oodi Central Library is notable as...
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - a nearly zero-energy public space co-designed with residents
        - the world's largest book archive
        - a private members-only library
        - a university research library

  - id: sdg13_q1
    text: What does SDG 13 call for?
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - Urgent action to combat climate change and its impacts
        - Universal access to clean water
        - Gender equality in education
        - Reduced inequality among countries

  - id: sdg13_q2
    text: Thammasat University Library's award-winning green program is built around...
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - the circular economy (From Waste to Wealth)
        - banning printed books
        - solar-powered bookmobiles only
        - closing the library to save energy

  - id: sdg13_q3
    text: A seed library primarily helps a community by...
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - sharing and tracking seeds for local growing
        - selling rare plants
        - storing grain reserves
        - replacing public gardens
